  "checks": [
    "CC1: verified the primitive finite Fourier transform at units and nonunits, the reduction-kernel argument, finite Parseval, Gaussian derivative sign and epsilon=tau/(i^a sqrt(N)). The Mellin formula has the factor one-half and exponent (s+a)/2. The principal conductor-one case separately removes the theta constant and retains its completed poles at zero and one.",
    "CC2: four mean-zero periodic primitives give the displayed product s(s+1)...(s+4), remainder exponent -s-5, O(N^5) primitive bound, and absolute convergence for Re(s)>-4. The principal Euler factors have polynomial conductor growth. Euler products give the stated fixed lower bound and exact von Mangoldt logarithmic derivative on Re(s)>1.",
    "CC3: checked all disk radii against the available strip and the QR15 Blaschke estimate. The final text uses the literal |Im(rho)-t|<=1 window; sqrt(5)<5/2 puts every such critical-strip zero inside the controlled disk. Counting analytic multiplicity, finiteness and conversion to log(N(|t|+2)) are valid uniformly.",
    "CC4: checked QW14 nonvanishing at one, positivity of paired alternating-zeta terms, and the 3+4cos(theta)+cos(2theta) boundary contradiction. At nonzero height the shifted square-character L-function has no pole, so its possible zero only strengthens the contradiction. The primitive functional equation gives exactly a simple zero at zero for nonprincipal even characters and no other zeros in the stated left strip.",
    "CC5: checked that the QR17/QR18 positivity arguments apply to actual Dirichlet characters using only the new local expansion, Euler derivative and principal pole, without an assumed LFam instance. Same-modulus character multiplication and real conjugation give simplicity and uniqueness across the modulus. The final text explicitly shrinks the constant to pass from the open ell_N strip to the source closed strip with log(N(|t|+2)).",
    "CC5: checked the NoExc quantifiers: c depends only on c0, before N, chi, lambda and the zero. Taking c<=min(b,c0,1) also handles every zero with Re(rho)<=0 automatically, so the literal pt_zero_free source with only Re(rho)<1 is supplied. The real nonprincipal zero-exclusion premise is retained.",
    "CC6: inversion preserves primitivity; the primitive functional equation reflects rho to 1-rho for chi^{-1}, without assuming conjugation symmetry for a complex character. The same real-character exclusion applies to the inverse, and lambda+log(5)<=3lambda yields the stated low-zero denominator bound.",
    "CC7: verified the low-height O(lambda) multiplicity count with reciprocal size O(lambda), and the higher unit-interval harmonic sum. The resulting C2(lambda+log T)^2 bound is uniform for T>=1 and its constant may depend on the retained exclusion c0.",
    "CC8: checked QR20 with full floor endpoints including integer u; independently selected upper and lower good heights; the deleted-ordinate measure; the horizontal logarithmic-derivative bound; and extension of the right edge by at most one unit. The functional equation at Re(s)=-1/2 reflects to Re(s)=3/2, while the direct gamma-series bound controls both fixed shifted real parts.",
    "CC8: checked the pole at one, the negative sign of every multiplicity-weighted zero residue, and the residue b0-e0 log(u) at zero. The local expansion bounds b0 by the explicit low-zero reciprocal sum plus O(log(N+2)), retaining possible zeros arbitrarily close to zero. Replacing good heights by the strict |Im(rho)|<T cutoff costs only the stated error. This is exactly PI.ExplicitFormulaWith, and it needs no real-zero exclusion.",
